WEBVTT

00:00:00.319 --> 00:00:02.699
Revenue Execution is built for teams closing

00:00:02.699 --> 00:00:04.939
up to 25,000 deals a year.

00:00:05.399 --> 00:00:10.099
Closing more? Talk to us, and we’ll set up reporting for your volume.

00:00:10.754 --> 00:00:12.934
First, give yourself access.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:17.554
Open your own user, and edit its permission set assignments.

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:23.141
Add Revenue Execution Configuration Health and Revenue Execution Viewer, and save.

00:00:23.685 --> 00:00:28.565
Then open Revenue Execution from the App Launcher, and choose Admin / Setup.

00:00:33.686 --> 00:00:35.866
Admin / Setup opens on “Get started”:

00:00:35.866 --> 00:00:38.941
every setup step, in the order that works.

00:00:38.941 --> 00:00:41.352
“Next” marks the step to do now.

00:00:41.352 --> 00:00:45.532
Choose “Show how” to see its steps, with the Setup path ready to copy.

00:00:49.086 --> 00:00:52.819
To report on another field, open “Configure Fields”.

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:57.894
Open “Deal value”, and choose your field, such as annual recurring revenue.

00:00:57.894 --> 00:01:01.102
“Preview” shows what changes before anything is saved.

00:01:01.102 --> 00:01:03.900
“Save”, check the change, and confirm.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.380
Every dashboard now uses it.

00:01:09.719 --> 00:01:12.219
Next, give your team access.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:17.034
Everyone who uses the dashboards needs Revenue Execution Viewer.

00:01:17.034 --> 00:01:20.506
Open each person, and edit their permission set assignments.

00:01:20.506 --> 00:01:23.666
Add Revenue Execution Viewer, and save.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:27.587
Back in Admin / Setup, “Recheck” confirms it.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.947
Team Performance follows the Manager set on each user.

00:01:34.452 --> 00:01:37.630
Get started shows the fields your Viewers can’t read yet.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.490
Give them Read access with a permission set your

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.307
company owns, and assign it to every Viewer.

00:01:43.307 --> 00:01:46.067
Use “Copy” to take these steps with you.

00:01:46.352 --> 00:01:48.592
Then “Recheck”, and you’re ready.

00:01:52.219 --> 00:01:56.210
“Health” checks access and settings, with the fix on each row.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:59.350
No failures and no warnings means setup is done.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:04.850
Info rows, like these for optional Deal Alerts, don’t affect the dashboards.

00:02:08.352 --> 00:02:12.072
Your team now sees its own deals, read as each person,

00:02:12.072 --> 00:02:14.966
with nothing changed in Salesforce.

00:02:14.966 --> 00:02:16.855
Start where deals are stuck.

00:02:16.855 --> 00:02:20.186
The how-to videos show each dashboard.

00:02:23.386 --> 00:02:27.669
Optional: Deal Alerts emails owners when deals slip.

00:02:27.669 --> 00:02:30.461
It stays off until you turn it on.

00:02:30.461 --> 00:02:34.081
“Preview” shows who would get what, before anything is sent.

00:02:34.547 --> 00:02:40.447
That’s setup. Every step is at revenue.opsgs.com.
